p.src:
The time scale is the first real structure: $\begin{aligned}
T_{\text{insurance}} &> 30 \ \text{years},\\
T_{\text{uncertain}} &\approx 3\text{--}4 \ \text{years}.\end{aligned}$ The two lines belong together. Mike’s insurance career lasts more than thirty years, but he says he did not know what he was doing for the first three or four. The early confusion is not edited out of the mechanism.

